      "details": "### Summary\n\nThe GitHub Action bundled with Black can read the version from `tool.black.required-version` if `use_pyproject` is set to True. This version is not validated and therefore can be used to execute untrusted code in the context of a victim's repository.\n\n### Details\n\nThis is similar to the previous CVE-2026-31900. The value in `tool.black.required-version` is accepted as the version to be installed by the action without validation.\n\n### Proof of concept\n\nReproduction requires a victim to use Black's GitHub Action with `use_pyproject: true`. The attacker would then issue a PR to the victim's repository with `pyproject.toml` edited so that Black points to a malicious repository.\n\n### Impact\n\nThis is a remote code execution vulnerability impacting users using the GitHub Action bundled with psf/black and using the `use_pyproject: true` setting.",
      "id": "GHSA-cg8m-r9f2-5wm2",
      "modified": "2026-10-22T16:30:30.132713769Z",
      "published": "2026-10-22T16:18:57Z",
